{
 "design": "Gate 0 v3 \u2014 frontal-face-present vs face-absent, single-source, SUSTAINED-SHOT and MOTION-MATCHED",
 "supersedes": "gate0_v2_stimuli.json (D021), which is retained unchanged as the historical record",
 "amendment": "D023(g), recorded 2026-07-30 BEFORE any Gate 0 brain data exists (zero v2/v3 runs completed)",
 "why": "The v2 set was measured on CPU (notebooks/gate0_v2_preflight.json) and failed two checks. (1) MOTION CONFOUND: frame-difference energy FACE 0.914 vs NONFACE 3.039, two-sided permutation p=0.0008, with 11/15 NONFACE clips above the FACE maximum. Because spatial_z subtracts the whole-brain mean and the EBA proxy is the motion-sensitive lateral occipitotemporal complex, that asymmetry can inflate both the primary statistic and the G3 margin, and G4 cannot detect it because motion survives video-only. (2) SHOT FRAGMENTATION: clips averaged 2.20 (FACE) and 1.53 (NONFACE) shot changes per 10 s, with 10/15 FACE clips cutting inside the first 2.5 s \u2014 the region V-JEPA2 over-weights, since it clamps to 4 s and feeds 217/1280 frames as duplicates of frame 0. D021's curation sampled a face detector every 5 s and was structurally blind to sub-5 s cuts. GATE-0.md's G5 pre-registered covariate matching 'after reselection', so this executes a clause already written rather than inventing one.",
 "clip_dur_s": 10,
